      "writtenOn": "2023-02-08T15:10:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the first time I\u0027m aware of in Skia to use a single triangle to cover the entire render target. Historically we\u0027ve always just drawn a quad as two triangles. This likely stemmed from these draws being issued from `DrawRect` operations at a high-level.\n\nWhat are your impressions of this technique vs. the two triangle approach? It would be nice to use a consistent strategy across the backends that have to do a draw blit, but that could easily mean we update the Metal backend to do it this way as well.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 101,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "7c1fcdb7a74edb3d64a32f63a41c6da834260196",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4e5bbf9c_c16946b7",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnResourceProvider.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 101,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-09T16:35:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The recommended way of doing fullscreen pass nowadays is using 1 big triangle instead of 2 triangles AFAIK. This article has some explanations: https://wallisc.github.io/rendering/2021/04/18/Fullscreen-Pass.html\n\nThe fragment shaders would be executed twice unnecessarily along the diagonal edge if 2 triangles were used. That\u0027s because of helper shader invocations typically running in a group of 4 to compute derivatives.\n\nFor graphite\u0027s texture copying shader, I imagine the performance win by using 1 big triangle is rather small. But a performance win, even small is always better than nothing. Nevertheless, the bigger the texture\u0027s resolution is, the more performance gain would be get from 1 triangle vs 2 triangles.",
      "parentUuid": "8d6344d9_f1603280",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 101,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 101,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "7c1fcdb7a74edb3d64a32f63a41c6da834260196",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8d55da8_149f30ba",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnResourceProvider.cpp",
